message: "Cite this package by title, author, and version until a DOI is assigned. CC BY 4.0 covers scientific text and metadata only; code, schemas, and tests are Copyright 2026 Ivan Kotov, all rights reserved, with no license grant."
title: "Continuity Instrument (CI): Evidence-Bound Measurement of Governed Continuity in Long-Lived AI Systems, v1.0"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kotov"
    given-names: "Ivan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6002-9845"
url: "https://ivankotov.eu/corpus-map/"
abstract: >-
  Continuity Instrument (CI) v1.0.0 source/reference package: a branch-aware,
  evidence-bound specification and deterministic reference transformation for
  recording governed continuity in long-lived AI systems. Evidence-bound
  continuity age or formation depth is represented as a vector rather than
  wall-clock age. R157 is open-synthetic predecessor evidence; frozen R160 and
  R161 local-evaluator attempts did not meet their qualification thresholds.
  The package does not establish entity identity, personhood, general
  evaluator validity, provider attestation, operational approval, or
  scientific qualification.
keywords:
  - "Continuity Instrument"
  - "governed continuity"
  - "evidence-bound measurement"
  - "long-lived AI systems"
  - "AI governance"
  - "provenance"
  - "formation depth"
  - "independent review"
